From 6b742af996378865b1090b4fcba74c4d6a842b57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darkmaniac7 <31073889+darkmaniac7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:06:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] firmware: per-step timing telemetry; host: passive
 snapshot, full-line replies

firmware (marker fw=lab-psr1-timing1, fw=lab-psr1-timing1-debug in the
debug build): every step of the glitch timeline records the start and end
of its call and whether it succeeded. After the shot, before "glitch
done", it prints one line per step:

  timing i=<n> scheduled=<us> act=<n> arg=<n> start=<us> end=<us> ok=<0|1>

Nothing is printed inside the step loop. On one bench this showed that a
PMBus write takes about 47 us, and that the PEX_RST release waits for a
VOUT_COMMAND write still running at t = 0 (td +81 with pw 36 released at
+59 us; the standard train at td -60 released on time). The table is in
docs/TIMING_DIAGNOSTIC.md.

host/ga100vfi/glitch.py: Card.cmd(until=...) waits for the newline that
ends the completion line, so a USB packet that splits "glitch done" from
its fields no longer turns a shot into a NACK.

host/passive_snapshot.py: read-only BAR0 observer (FUSECTRL, GFW, DSOV,
CRC, privilege mask). It stops at the first 0xBADF value, I/O error,
all-ones read, GFW still booting or DSOV other than 0 or 1, and never
writes.

Tests: host/test_passive_snapshot.py, host/test_serial_response.py.
